WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.071
♪♪

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.439
-All right, guys,
if you're in New York,

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.741
you have to go to
the greatest place to eat,

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.576
and that is Katz's Deli.

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.478
That's where we are.
It's the best food.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.580
It's been around
for many generations.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.881
-How old is here?

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.784
-I'll let Jake, the owner,
talk to you about this.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:19.351
Jake?
-Oh!

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:21.120
-Hey!
-Hey, guys.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.289
How is everything?
Welcome, guys.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.691
So, we've been here 132 years.

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:26.893
-Ooh!
-Yeah.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.728
We're known for, like,
pastrami, corned beef,

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.064
brisket, turkey,
matzah ball soup.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.498
We're gonna feed
the crap out of you.

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:33.632
Can I tell you that?

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:34.667
I don't know if I'm allowed
to say that.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.169
-Yeah, can you say that.
Absolutely.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.571
Also, have you ever seen
"When Harry Met Sally"?

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.973
-No.
-No?

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:42.575
-"Harry Met Sally"?
-No.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.910
-No, there's a famous scene
in that movie...

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.146
-That's from this restaurant.
So it's in that movie.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.181
This is a famous place,
the one and only Katz's.

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:50.383
Let's gets some food!
-Yeah.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.918
-Let's do it!
Yeah!

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:56.756
-Whoa!
-Over here.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:58.091
-Very heavy.
-Whoa!

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.359
-What's this?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:03.396
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.032
-Is it for, like, one man, or --
-Yeah, yeah, that's yours.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.433
-Okay.
-All right, that one is --

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:08.901
-In America, this is what
we eat for breakfast.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:10.803
-Don't let me stop you.
Let's go. Dig in.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.605
Let's go, dig in.
Don't be shy.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.108
-Look at that.
-You're good.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.409
-Pastrami?
-Pastrami.

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:19.645
-But no veggies?
-No veggies.

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.447
No. Are you kidding me?
No.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:25.518
-Try it.
-What do you think?

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.653
-Mm.
-So, put some mustard on those.

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:28.988
-Ooh.
-No ketchup.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.256
-No ketchup?
-Get out of here.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.125
Get out of here with ketchup.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.993
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.329
-What is the go-to food
in Korea?

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.831
-Spicy fried chicken.
-What if you, like,

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.633
late at night, and you feel like
having a snack?

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:41.634
-Chicken.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.801
-Chicken is the way to go,
right?

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:45.705
-Chicken and beer.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.740
-Chicken and beer.
-Cheers.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.275
-Cheers, come on.
-Cheers.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:50.409
-Guys, you know what
I want to do?

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.478
Let's go make some sandwiches

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:52.478
and give it to
the people out there.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:53.479
All right, let's go.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:57.516
♪♪

00:01:57.516 --> 00:02:00.052
-Okay. So I need your help
making these sandwiches.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.988
I need you
on waiter service duty.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:04.323
-Any advice how to cut this?
-Yeah.

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:07.259
So, you got to use the back
of the knife like that.

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:09.495
Nice, beautiful --
-Ooh!

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.697
-Oh.
-Skinny.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.366
-Beautiful pieces of meat
like that, right?

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.635
So, we got some sandwiches here.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:18.004
-Mmm!
-Thank you.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.339
-When these are ready,
just yell, "Order up."

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:22.441
-Order up!
-And then you come, you grab it.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:23.977
-Oh, yeah.
-And you book it.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.111
-Order up!
-Order up!

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:29.048
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.852
-BTS made it for you.
-Order up!

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:36.021
-Order up!
-Order up!

00:02:36.021 --> 00:02:37.923
-Order up!

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:40.193
-I'm coming, I'm coming,
I'm coming, I'm coming.

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:42.261
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:43.962
Me and BTS.
Please enjoy.

00:02:43.962 --> 00:02:45.965
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:53.105
♪♪

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.206
Good work.

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:55.841
-Let's go.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:58.177
-Guys, enough fooling around.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:01.413
You are going to perform
at Grand Central right now.

00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:02.815
Tonight.
That's legendary.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:03.983
So enough with the sandwiches.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.185
Let's go to Grand Central
and put on a show!

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.187
Let's do it!
Yeah!

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:09.422
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:19.231
♪♪

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:20.566
♪♪

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:24.870
-Hi. I'm Fran Lebowitz,
and this is my subway story.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.207
I was on the subway, sitting
across from a woman with a baby.

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:30.409
The baby had a pacifier
in its mouth.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.111
The pacifier
fell out of the baby's mouth

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.813
onto the floor
of the subway car.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:36.683
The woman bent down,
picked it up, went like this,

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:38.484
and put it back
in the baby's mouth.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:41.020
I thought to myself, "Either
that baby is going to drop dead

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:44.090
right here or that baby will
live to be a thousand years old,

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.893
because he's now immunized from
every germ on the planet Earth."

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:50.596
If I dropped the Hope Diamond
on the floor of a subway car,

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:52.098
it would stay there.

